==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Elder Egg: N000''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ape Lord Luza''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
With its combination of stats and abilities, Ape Lord Luza is a powerful backliner and a definitive answer to Relic enemies, especially those it can outrange such as [[M. Ost]] or those it can tank like [[Golem Sunfish]]. Its most notable targets obviously include Relic-type Behemoths, namely [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]] (with its Surge Immunity) and [[Ultima Beast Naala]] (on higher Crown difficulties). Its Warp/Surge Immunity also helps counter [[Spiritual Yulala (Enemy)|Spiritual Yulala]] in [[Infernal Tower]] [[Infernal Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]], as well as [[Esoteric Uril (Enemy)|Esoteric Uril]] in [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|Floor 50]]. Outside of these particular targets, it still works against many Relics and has good generalist stats, while its second Multi-Hit pierces 150 ahead from its 400 range to snipe Behemoths from afar. Note that [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] tends to have better compatibility against longer-ranged Behemoths (460), and that Luza may not always manage to land both hits, as they occur in a rapid succession and cover different ranges, causing the second hit to miss if the first knocks the enemy back.

